  "notes": "⚠ **This entry is a holding placement, and the research says so.** The roadmap asks for a `chicago-bounce` archetype for this act and `data/genres/` does not contain one; they sit under `boom-bap` because this is the file that owns the Chicago soul-sample axis, not because the parameters fit. Move it on creation of the archetype. What the research does give is unusually specific. The signature is \"a shuffled/triplet ride-cymbal or open-hat carrier… not a straight 8th hat — the whole groove gallops\", authored as `swing` on the 8th grid at **0.67**, effectively full triplet and by far the heaviest in this batch, with the ride and hand percussion as a standing 3–5 hits a bar and `openHat.prob` 0.5 across every `&`. ⚠ The ride is a `percs` lane rather than a hat base because `hihat.base` has no triplet value the generator reads; the shuffle lives in `session.swing` instead. The two tonal poles are authored directly — B minor and F♯ minor at equal weight, with A/A♭ major on the up cuts — because the research lists them per track. The source is P-Funk rather than soul-jazz, so the bass is a real player: `independent_riff` at 0.5 with five passing tones and `anticipationProb` 0.35, \"Midwest funk-bass rather than a sustained sub\". \"Low instrumental note density — the density is in the voices\" is `melody.densityPerBar` 2–5 with `structure` `call_response` and a hook the countermelody doubles in octaves, for the group chant sung by all four in unison. ⚠ `bpm` is the research's **notated** band, 132–146 centred on 139. bpmdatabase reports the same two singles at 70 and 94 — exactly half — so the spine is unambiguous but the notation is not, and the research marks the choice `[LOW-CONF]`. Which of the two notations this model should carry is the **INFERRED** decision here, and it is the first thing to revisit: at the halved reading every density above would need doubling. The ride-shuffle grammar itself is also `[LOW-CONF]` per the research. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 48 to 43 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 44 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 5.",
